# Tailwind class strings

`pnpm lint` fails on non-canonical or conflicting utilities. Write the short form the first time.

## Canonical (suggestCanonicalClasses)

Collapse utilities that set the same thing:

- `px-4 py-4` → `p-4`
- `translate-x-2 translate-y-2` → `translate-2` (`active:translate-[2px]` for the arcade press)
- `-translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2` → `-translate-1/2`
- `text-3xl leading-tight` → `text-3xl/tight`
- `min-h-[4.25rem]` → `min-h-17` (use the spacing scale, not arbitrary px/rem)

Do not stack a shorthand with the long form it already covers.

## Conflicts (cssConflict)

Never put two utilities on the same element that set the same CSS properties in the same variant:

```tsx
// BAD — both set outline-style and outline-width
className="outline outline-2 outline-go"

// GOOD
className="outline-2 outline-go"
```

Mutually exclusive styles belong in separate `cn()` / ternary branches, not in one string:

```tsx
// BAD
className="flex grid"
className="bg-card bg-elevated"

// GOOD
className={cn("flex", selected ? "bg-elevated" : "bg-card")}
```

`outline-2` already includes the outline style. Do not also add `outline`.
